      Q. 1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَرْمَدَ</span></b>  <i>He plastered</i> a pool, (S, L,) or a
tank, or cistern, (L,) <i>with the burnt stones called</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَرْمَدٌ</span>: (S, L:) or <i>he plastered thickly.</i> (TA, art.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كلس</span>.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>He constructed</i> a building <i>with such
stones.</i> (L.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  [<i>He smeared</i> a garment <i>with
saffron, or perfume.</i> See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُقَرْمَدٌ</span>.]

